": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120198832202125322", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick Google also showed a Three.js reconstruction of a building from planning drawings. For the video example, I’d change the camera angle to see whether the geometry holds up beyond the original view.", "url": "https://x.com/briefing_block_/status/2120306599428538833"}, {"author_id": "1219767630", "created_at": "2026-11-10T23:52:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120303665647087912"], "id": "2120303665647087912", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120198832202125322", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick Carbon's ability to reinterpret video in 3D is a fascinating step forward in AI creativity", "url": "https://x.com/kimindiehacker/status/2120303665647087912"}, {"author_id": "343877206", "created_at": "2026-11-10T23:42:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120301215192166569"], "id": "2120301215192166569", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120198832202125322", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick Agree. Having a model that thinks differently is useful as a second opinion, especially for reviews.", "url": "https://x.com/smobilefactory/status/2120301215192166569"}, {"author_id": "358333297", "created_at": "2026-11-10T23:16:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120294522156666909"], "id": "2120294522156666909", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 20, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120198832202125322", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick i mean even a model that thinks differntly still mirrors the state you prompt it from, stressed in stressed out, nobody benchmarks that part", "url": "https://x.com/manujagro/status/2120294522156666909"}, {"author_id": "2104993200490393600", "created_at": "2026-11-10T23:07:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120292190630899748"], "id": "2120292190630899748", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120198832202125322", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick Having a model that thinks differently is underrated. I already run the same prompt through two models and use whatever both agree on. A third opinion makes that even better.", "url": "https://x.com/ceobrendan/status/2120292190630899748"}, {"author_id": "1689098925159149569", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:35:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120284230139928742"], "id": "2120284230139928742", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120198832202125322", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick I tried Carbon with a short video clip too, and it generated a 3D model in WebGL in under 2 minutes. It’s definitely faster than Argon for that task.", "url": "https://x.com/chengfu588728/status/2120284230139928742"}, {"author_id": "1241772314", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:25:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120281685774553212"], "id": "2120281685774553212", "in_reply_to_user_id": "14130366", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 17, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120280429680812198", "type": "quoted"}, {"id": "2120211703006962098", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@sundarpichai @emollick https://t.co/1mGSJ48Cgf", "url": "https://x.com/sunset_evm/status/2120281685774553212"}, {"author_id": "996493767791251459", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:23:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120281305707581504"], "id": "2120281305707581504", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120198832202125322", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick I feel it can understand other models neuralese and translate it to human-ish language, which is kinda cool.", "url": "https://x.com/sohakes/status/2120281305707581504"}, {"author_id": "1690764692904419328", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:21:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120280813530911050"], "id": "2120280813530911050", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120198832202125322", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick What are the weaknesses", "url": "https://x.com/S4mur_AI/status/2120280813530911050"}, {"author_id": "2107556122005540865", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:08:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120277362713440672"], "id": "2120277362713440672", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 38, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120198832202125322", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick \"Thinks differently\" is the part I'd want to see on a real task. If it makes different mistakes than Claude, that alone makes it worth running as a second opinion.", "url": "https://x.com/AiXAntho/status/2120277362713440672"}, {"author_id": "709866091892367361", "created_at": "2026-11-10T21:49:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120272775797416258"], "id": "2120272775797416258", "in_reply_to_user_id": 